.TH "ROTBYTE\-NOTIFY" "7" "2026\-11\-08" "rotbyte 1.4.0" "rotbyte Manual"
.SH NAME
rotbyte\-notify \- configure email notifications for rotbyte
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set up \f[CR]rotbyte \-\-notify email\f[R] to get an email health report
after every full re\-verify, plus an alert when a scheduled quick scan
finds a problem.
This is a one\-time setup.
Once it\(cqs done, notifications work automatically.
.PP
Email can only report on scans that actually run.
To also be alerted when scans \f[B]stop running\f[R] (a sleeping Mac, an
unmounted volume, a schedule broken by an upgrade), add healthchecks.io
monitoring (\f[CR]rotbyte \-\-docs healthchecks\f[R]).
You can use both at once with \f[CR]\-\-notify email,healthchecks\f[R].
.SS Quick start
.IP
.EX
rotbyte \-\-notify\-setup email
.EE
.PP
You\(cqll be prompted, in order, for:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]SMTP host\f[R]
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]SMTP port\f[R], default \f[CR]587\f[R]
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]Username\f[R], which is your email address
.IP "4." 3
\f[B]Password\f[R], which must be an app password (see below)
.IP "5." 3
\f[B]Send alerts to\f[R], which defaults to your username
.IP "6." 3
\f[B]Send alerts from\f[R], which defaults to your username.
Set it to an alias if you want alerts to come from a different address.
.PP
Port \f[CR]587\f[R] uses STARTTLS and port \f[CR]465\f[R] uses implicit
TLS.
Both verify the server\(cqs certificate.
A test email is sent at the end to confirm everything works.
.PP
\f[B]Where things are stored:\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]SMTP password:\f[R] your OS credential store.
That\(cqs the macOS Keychain (service \f[CR]rotbyte\-notify\f[R],
account \f[CR]<username>\(at<smtp host>\f[R]), Windows Credential
Manager, or libsecret on Linux.
If no credential store is available, the password is saved in the config
file with \f[CR]0600\f[R] permissions, and setup prints a warning.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Everything else:\f[R] a config file with \f[CR]0600\f[R]
permissions:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
macOS: \f[CR]\(ti/Library/Application Support/rotbyte/notify.conf\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Linux: \f[CR]\(ti/.config/rotbyte/notify.conf\f[R] (or
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rotbyte/notify.conf\f[R])
.IP \(bu 2
Windows: \f[CR]%USERPROFILE%\(rs.config\(rsrotbyte\(rsnotify.conf\f[R]
.RE
.PP
The same file holds the healthchecks.io settings in their own section.
Setting up one backend never changes the other.
.PP
